---
title: HTML Attributes
description: Reference for all data-dnd-* HTML attributes set and consumed by the library.
---

# HTML Attributes

The library sets these attributes automatically — you don't need to add them manually. However, knowing them is useful for CSS targeting and debugging.

---

## Data Attributes

| Attribute                   | Set by | Purpose |
|-----------------------------|--------|---------|
| `data-dnd-droppable`        | `DndDroppable` | Presence marker on the container element. Used by the scroll controller to detect scrollable droppables. Carries no value. |
| `data-dnd-drop-id`          | `DndDroppable` | Container ID string — used by internal helpers for DOM lookup of the container element. |
| `data-dnd-layout`           | `DndDroppable` | `'vertical'` / `'horizontal'` / `'grid'` for sortable containers. Drives the built-in default flex direction (vertical/horizontal only); absent on `target()` containers. |
| `data-dnd-scroll`           | User | Opt-in auto-scroll for **non-droppable** scroll containers (e.g. a page wrapper or a kanban board `div`). Add manually to any scrollable element that should participate in auto-scroll. |
| `data-dnd-slot`             | `DndDraggable` | Presence marker on the slot wrapper element. Useful for `closest('[data-dnd-slot]')` traversal. Carries no value. |
| `data-dnd-draggable`        | `DndDraggable` | Presence marker on the draggable element. Useful for `closest('[data-dnd-draggable]')` traversal. Carries no value. |
| `data-dnd-drag-id`          | `DndDraggable` | Item ID string — set alongside `data-dnd-draggable` to identify the element. |
| `data-dnd-handle`           | User | Marks an element as the drag handle. When present anywhere inside a `DndDraggable`, dragging only starts from handle elements; `data-dnd-no-drag` is ignored. |
| `data-dnd-no-drag`          | User | Disables drag initiation for this element and its descendants. Ignored when `data-dnd-handle` is used. |
| `data-dnd-preview`          | `DndPreview` | Presence marker on a preview (placeholder) slot element. |
| `data-dnd-preview-position` | `DndPreview` | Numeric position of the preview — used by internal helpers to locate a specific placeholder. |
| `data-dnd-dragged-element`  | `DndProvider` | Marks the ghost element (the floating `div` that follows the cursor). |

---

### Auto-scroll

Auto-scroll activates automatically for any `DndDroppable` element that has scrollable overflow (`overflow: auto` / `overflow: scroll`). `DndDroppable` sets `data-dnd-droppable` on its root element, and the scroll controller uses that marker to discover scrollable containers at runtime. No extra configuration is required.

### Disabling drag on child elements

Add `data-dnd-no-drag` to any element inside a `DndDraggable` to let it receive native pointer events without triggering a drag:

```svelte
<DndDraggable id={item.id} position={index}>
  <button data-dnd-no-drag onclick={() => alert("clicked!")}>Click me</button>
  {item.label}
</DndDraggable>
```

### Restricting drag to a handle

Add `data-dnd-handle` to one or more elements inside a `DndDraggable`. When at least one handle is present, dragging starts only from those elements — everything else is automatically blocked:

```svelte
<DndDraggable id={column.id} position={index}>
  <h2 data-dnd-handle>&#x2630; Drag here</h2>
  <div>clicks here won't drag</div>
</DndDraggable>
```

Multiple handles are supported — just add the attribute to each:

```svelte
<DndDraggable id={item.id} position={index}>
  <header data-dnd-handle>&#x2630; Top handle</header>
  <p>content</p>
  <footer data-dnd-handle>&#x2630; Bottom handle</footer>
</DndDraggable>
```
